ACID Properties - 

A transaction is a sequence of operations treated as a single unit of work.

A = Atomicity
"All or Nothing"

Atomicity ensures that either all operations in a transaction are executed or none are.

C = Consistency

Consistency ensures that a transaction preserves all database rules, constraints, and integrity requirements.

I = Isolation

Isolation ensures that concurrent transactions do not affect each other's execution.

D = Durability

Durability guarantees that committed transactions are permanently stored and cannot be lost.

ACID properties are Atomicity, Consistency, Isolation, and Durability. They ensure transactions execute reliably, maintain data integrity, handle concurrent access safely, and preserve committed data even after failures.

After ACID, interviewers almost always move to Isolation Levels: Read Uncommitted, Read Committed, Repeatable Read, Serializable

