Joins - 
A JOIN is used to combine rows from two or more tables based on a related column.	

1. INNER JOIN

Returns only matching records from both tables.

2. LEFT JOIN (LEFT OUTER JOIN)

Returns:

All rows from the left table
Matching rows from the right table

3. RIGHT JOIN (RIGHT OUTER JOIN)

Returns:

All rows from the right table
Matching rows from the left table

4. FULL OUTER JOIN

Returns:

All rows from both tables
Matching rows where possible
NULL where no match exists


5. CROSS JOIN

Produces the Cartesian Product.

Every row of table A combines with every row of table B.

6. SELF JOIN

A table joined with itself.

Joins are used to combine data from multiple tables based on a related column. Common types include INNER JOIN, which returns matching rows; LEFT JOIN, which returns all rows from the left table and matching rows from the right table; RIGHT JOIN, which returns all rows from the right table; FULL OUTER JOIN, which returns all rows from both tables; CROSS JOIN, which creates a Cartesian product; and SELF JOIN, where a table is joined with itself.

